1. THE a2/a3 PER-BIT BIAS IS A COROLLARY OF THE FORCED Maj CONDITION
   Allowed (a2_i,a3_i) states are {(v,v),(~v,v),(~v,~v)}, each 1/3.
   => p(a2_i = 1) = 1/3 if v_i=1 else 2/3 ;  p(a3_i = 1) = 2/3 if v_i=1 else 1/3.
   predicted vs measured over all 1920 (context,bit) cells:
   a2: mean residual +0.00024  rms 0.01593   (binomial sd 0.01613) -> ratio 0.99
   a3: mean residual +0.00054  rms 0.01625   (binomial sd 0.01613) -> ratio 1.01
   spread-inflation of pooled p across contexts, predicted (1/6)/0.01710 = 9.74
   => the pooled "biases" at bits 25/29 are 60-context sampling noise in v, not structure.

