3. DETECTION POWER ON c3 (this bounds any speedup that could be hiding)
   n=68680 in 40 contexts (1717 per context).
   (i) CONCENTRATED deficit (one frequency / one predictor):
       T(beta)=sum_c n_c|phi_c|^2 ~ Gamma(40,1).  A 4.5-sigma excess is T-40 = 28.5,
       i.e. mean |phi_c(beta)|^2 = 4.14e-04.  Entropy deficit of a +-beta pair = |phi|^2/ln2:
       ==> any SINGLE-FREQUENCY deficit above 5.98e-04 bits (= 2^0.0 speedup) would have shown.
   (ii) BROADLY SPREAD deficit: aggregate collision test on c3 mod 2^b, within context.
       b= 8: 231251 collisions vs 230333 expected (1.91 sd).  Total deficit inside this
             2^8 subgroup = +0.0029 bits; 4-sigma upper limit 0.0060 bits.
       b=12: 15207 collisions vs 14396 expected (6.76 sd).  Total deficit inside this
             2^12 subgroup = +0.0406 bits; 4-sigma upper limit 0.0240 bits.
       b=16: 1424 collisions vs 900 expected (17.48 sd).  Total deficit inside this
             2^16 subgroup = +0.4203 bits; 4-sigma upper limit 0.0962 bits.
   (iii) MI noise floor: 2x2 tables, n=68680 -> E[MI_null]=1.05e-05 bits, 99.99%ile 1.59e-04 bits.
        per-bit probability resolution: sd(p)=0.00191, so |p-0.5|>0.0076 detectable.

