4. WHAT THE CONVOLUTION COSTS AN ATTACKER WHO RESTRICTS THE TABLE
   Suppose the policy stores roots only in a subset of density 2^-k (H(W3)=32-k).
   Then the table hit rate falls by 2^-k, so the lookups cost 2^k MORE swept a0,
   while c3 could at best gain 2^k.  Exactly zero-sum -- before the convolution,
   which additionally destroys the gain because phi_c3 = phi_W3 * phi_{s0(W4)}.
